## Security and operations

- Errors follow RFC 7807 (`application/problem+json` with `type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`).
- Every request gets an `X-Request-ID` (yours is kept); logs are JSON lines that carry it (`LOG_FORMAT`).
{% if spec.auth %}
- Passwords are hashed with scrypt (memory-hard, standard library).
{% endif %}
{% if spec.roles %}
- Roles: {% for r in spec.roles %}`{{ r.name }}`{% if not r.self_signup %} (given by an admin: `PATCH /auth/users/<id>/role`){% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. Admins (`ADMIN_EMAILS`) pass every role check.
{% endif %}
{% if spec.has("refresh_tokens") %}
- Refresh tokens: login returns `refresh_token`; `POST /auth/refresh` rotates it, and reusing an old one logs out every session of that login. `POST /auth/logout` revokes it.
{% endif %}
{% if spec.has("account_lockout") %}
- Account lockout: `LOCKOUT_ATTEMPTS` failed logins lock the account for `LOCKOUT_MINUTES` (423).
{% endif %}
{% if spec.has("audit_log") %}
- Audit log: every create, change, delete and action is written to `audit_logs`; admins read it at `GET /audit_logs/`. Entries cannot be changed or deleted.
{% endif %}
{% if spec.has("rate_limit") %}
- Rate limits (token bucket) on sign-up, login and custom actions, 429 with `Retry-After`. Set `REDIS_URL` to share them between server processes.
{% endif %}
{% if spec.actions | selectattr("locks") | list %}
- Actions that move money or stock lock their row (`SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` on Postgres) for the whole transaction.
{% endif %}

## Production (Docker + Postgres)

```bash
export SECRET_KEY=$(python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))")
make docker                 # runs migrations, then the server
```

The container runs as a non-root user and applies database migrations (`{{ stack.cmd.migrate }}`) on start.
After changing a model, create a migration with `make migration`.

## Configuration

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `ENV` | `dev`/`test` create tables automatically; `production` relies on migrations |
| `DATABASE_URL` | SQLite or Postgres URL |
{% if spec.auth or stack.name == "django" %}
| `SECRET_KEY` | signs login tokens; **required** in production |
{% endif %}
{% if spec.auth %}
| `ADMIN_EMAILS` | comma-separated emails with admin rights |
{% endif %}
| `CORS_ORIGINS` | comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the API |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | e.g. `INFO`, `DEBUG` |

